  "notes": "SANYO ATV R2 (manufacturer SCBC, device R2, Realtek RTD285O), Android TV 9 (API 28),\nfirmware PTT1.201001.001 build 200, security patch 2020-11-05, 2 GB RAM, 1920x1080.\nFingerprint: SANYO/SANYO/R2:9/PTT1.201001.001/200:user/release-keys\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/sanyo-atv-r2/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/sanyo-atv-r2/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher is com.google.android.tvlauncher and Live TV is com.android.tv (Realtek RtkLiveTv),\nso the defaults in tools/restore.sh and launcher/build-and-install.sh work unchanged.\ncom.google.android.leanbacklauncher is also installed and claims HOME; it was left enabled as a fallback.\n\nNotes from this TV:\n- Leave alone: com.rtk.engmenu, com.realtek.factorytools, com.apps.factory.ui (factory menus),\ncom.apps.fivekey / smartkey / virtualkey and com.realtek.keyinterceptserver (remote keys),\ncom.realtek.tv.* / com.realtek.dtv (HDMI, AV, tuner inputs), com.apps.sys (SystemProvider).\n- Kept in use: Chromecast (com.google.android.apps.mediashell), Assistant (com.google.android.katniss),\nFastCast Miracast (com.creative.fastscreen.tv), Audio Link and PureSound.\n- Inputs: HDMI 1-3 and AV are TvInputService passthrough inputs; switching via\nTvContract.buildChannelUriForPassthroughInput() opens them in Live TV. HDMI200004 is a CEC child, skip it.\n- Android 9 only shows the Wi-Fi SSID to apps holding location permission (location is on by default here).\n- Over Wi-Fi ADB, streamed `adb install` of a ~45 MB APK failed silently; push to /data/local/tmp and `pm install` worked.\nSCBC / Realtek / Google telemetry and feedback",
